2025/11/13

This is a snapshot of the libion library from system/memory/libion
as of 2025/8, before that library was declared deprecated and the
functionality turned into NOPs.

While libion is no longer supported on newly released devices, it is
required for medias mainline modules -- which are required to function
on devices back to Android S. And those devices do still use libion for
their shared memory.

We have renamed the library "libion_legacy" to avoid any confusion while the
original no-longer-functional libion library is present in the build tree.
We also have limited the visibility of this legacy library so that it will not
be used by other components outside of the media stack.
